{"item_id": "B000R41LD4", "title": "Crosman RMCOIL Silicone Chamber Oil", "description": "This chamber oil is specifically designed and recommended for use on all Crosman Break-Barrel and Precharged Pneumatic (PCP) airguns and air rifles.", "text": "Crosman RMCOIL Silicone Chamber Oil This chamber oil is specifically designed and recommended for use on all Crosman Break-Barrel and Precharged Pneumatic (PCP) airguns and air rifles.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31938W3KB4L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R41LD4.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Crosman", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Airsoft, Air Guns & Slingshots", "Air Guns"]], "price": 8.95}}
{"item_id": "B000R4AHJI", "title": "Hammerli 850 AirMagnum air rifle", "description": "THE FASTEST CO2 RIFLE! The 850 AirMagnum is a high-tech, fixed barrel, 8-shot repeating rifle that features a uniform, rapid rate of fire at a velocity of 760 feet per second! This CO2 air rifle uses a smooth, bolt-action system with a rotary magazine that holds 8 lead pellets. Up to 200 shots can be fired from one 88g CO2 cylinder. Its all-weather polymer stock is ambidextrous with cheekpieces on both sides of a Monte Carlo stock and you'll keep your target clear and hands steady with the 850's fiber optic sights and checkered grips. The fiber-optic sights will help you acquire your target, but feel free to mount a scope on the 11mm dovetail rail. The checkering on the pistol grip and forearm will help you get a good grip while you plow shot after shot from this 8-shot repeater. This gun is everything you ever hoped for in a CO2 repeater! Note: The package contains the gun only. The scope and CO2 are sold separately.", "text": "Hammerli 850 AirMagnum air rifle THE FASTEST CO2 RIFLE! The 850 AirMagnum is a high-tech, fixed barrel, 8-shot repeating rifle that features a uniform, rapid rate of fire at a velocity of 760 feet per second! This CO2 air rifle uses a smooth, bolt-action system with a rotary magazine that holds 8 lead pellets. Up to 200 shots can be fired from one 88g CO2 cylinder. Its all-weather polymer stock is ambidextrous with cheekpieces on both sides of a Monte Carlo stock and you'll keep your target clear and hands steady with the 850's fiber optic sights and checkered grips. The fiber-optic sights will help you acquire your target, but feel free to mount a scope on the 11mm dovetail rail. The checkering on the pistol grip and forearm will help you get a good grip while you plow shot after shot from this 8-shot repeater. This gun is everything you ever hoped for in a CO2 repeater! Note: The package contains the gun only. The scope and CO2 are sold separately.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/217QDjFZw4L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R4AHJI.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Umarex", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Airsoft, Air Guns & Slingshots", "Air Guns", "Air Rifles"]], "price": 256.83}}
{"item_id": "B000R4HSW2", "title": "NcStar 4X20 Compact Air Scope/Blue Lens (SCA420B)", "description": "Maximize the performance of your firearm with the NcStar Tactical 4x20 air scope. Equipped with multicoated lenses that provide a crisp sight and a lightweight body, the scope is always ready for action.SpecificationsMagnification: 4xTube diameter: 0.75 inchesObjective diameter: 20mmField of view: 26.2 feet @ 100 yardsEye relief: 2.5 inchesExit pupil: 5mmReticle: PlexClick value: N/ALens coating: BlueMount included: Dovetail ringsExterior finish: Matte blackLength: 7.88 inchesWeight: 3.35 ounces", "text": "NcStar 4X20 Compact Air Scope/Blue Lens (SCA420B) Maximize the performance of your firearm with the NcStar Tactical 4x20 air scope. Equipped with multicoated lenses that provide a crisp sight and a lightweight body, the scope is always ready for action.SpecificationsMagnification: 4xTube diameter: 0.75 inchesObjective diameter: 20mmField of view: 26.2 feet @ 100 yardsEye relief: 2.5 inchesExit pupil: 5mmReticle: PlexClick value: N/ALens coating: BlueMount included: Dovetail ringsExterior finish: Matte blackLength: 7.88 inchesWeight: 3.35 ounces", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31dCCuRKMDL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R4HSW2.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "NcStar", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 9.99}}
{"item_id": "B000R58JM4", "title": "Stansport Backpacker's Air Mattress, Brown (72- X 29-Inch)", "description": "Designed for lightweight backpacking and camping, this air mattress from Stansport is made of laminated nylon with a polyurethane backing for durability. The mattress features six independent air chambers and is equipped with quick release valves for fast deflation. The mattress comes with a nylon stuff sack and a repair kit included.", "text": "Stansport Backpacker's Air Mattress, Brown (72- X 29-Inch) Designed for lightweight backpacking and camping, this air mattress from Stansport is made of laminated nylon with a polyurethane backing for durability. The mattress features six independent air chambers and is equipped with quick release valves for fast deflation. The mattress comes with a nylon stuff sack and a repair kit included.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41Mvp8vI4BL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R58JM4.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "StanSport", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Outdoor Gear", "Camping & Hiking", "Camp Bedding", "Air Mattresses"]], "price": 29.97}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NR8K", "title": "Cateye HL-EL530 LED Bicycle Headlight", "description": "Fifty percent brighter than Cateye's HL-EL500 model, this extra-bright one-LED white headlight generates 1,500 candlepower thanks to Cateye's OptiCube technology that optimizes lens and reflector brightness. It runs on four AA batteries and produces 90 hours of run time. Other features include side visibility and a tool-free mounting bracket.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye HL-EL530 LED Bicycle Headlight Fifty percent brighter than Cateye's HL-EL500 model, this extra-bright one-LED white headlight generates 1,500 candlepower thanks to Cateye's OptiCube technology that optimizes lens and reflector brightness. It runs on four AA batteries and produces 90 hours of run time. Other features include side visibility and a tool-free mounting bracket.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41XXms39ybL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NR8K.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Headlights"]]}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NR9O", "title": "Cateye HE-EL135 Sport OptiCube LED", "description": "Cat Eye HE-EL135 Sport OptiCube LED Headlights feature three superbright, white LEDs. Three superbright, white LEDs Batteries Included 80 candlepower 80 hou", "text": "Cateye HE-EL135 Sport OptiCube LED Cat Eye HE-EL135 Sport OptiCube LED Headlights feature three superbright, white LEDs. Three superbright, white LEDs Batteries Included 80 candlepower 80 hou", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41uMT87mCnL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NR9O.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Headlights"]], "price": 23.99}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NRAS", "title": "Cateye TL-LD500-R LED Bicycle Tail and Safety Light (Red)", "description": "This three red-LED tail light offers a constant mode and flashing mode. Powered by two AAA batteries, the light offers up to 100 hours of run time in flashing mode and 50 hours in constant mode. It mounts easily to any seat post or handlebar. A clothing clip is also included.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye TL-LD500-R LED Bicycle Tail and Safety Light (Red) This three red-LED tail light offers a constant mode and flashing mode. Powered by two AAA batteries, the light offers up to 100 hours of run time in flashing mode and 50 hours in constant mode. It mounts easily to any seat post or handlebar. A clothing clip is also included.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51B1dSRALGL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NRAS.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Taillights"]]}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NRBM", "title": "Cateye LD130 Taillight", "description": "Cat Eye LD130 Taillights feature 3 LEDs that last up to 150 hours of run time. Up to 150 hours of run time Includes batteries Includes Flex-Tight bracket that fit u", "text": "Cateye LD130 Taillight Cat Eye LD130 Taillights feature 3 LEDs that last up to 150 hours of run time. Up to 150 hours of run time Includes batteries Includes Flex-Tight bracket that fit u", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/518qyvZxT2L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NRBM.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "CATEYE", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Taillights"]], "price": 10.8}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NRDK", "title": "Cateye CC-VL510 Velo 5-Function Bicycle Computer", "description": "Accompanied by universal handlebar and front-fork-sensor mounts, this entry-level five-function bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed, trip distance, total distance, and 12/24-hour clock. Other features include tire setting in inches and centimeters, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR2032 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-32 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR2032 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye CC-VL510 Velo 5-Function Bicycle Computer Accompanied by universal handlebar and front-fork-sensor mounts, this entry-level five-function bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed, trip distance, total distance, and 12/24-hour clock. Other features include tire setting in inches and centimeters, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR2032 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-32 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR2032 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51rcjaiwMaL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NRDK.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "CATEYE", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Accessories", "Electronics & Gadgets", "Cycling Computers"]], "price": 20.91}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NRDU", "title": "Cateye CC-RD100 Strada 8-Function Bicycle Computer", "description": "Sleek, lightweight, and elegant, this slim bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed (up to 65 mph), average speed, trip distance, second-trip distance, total distance, elapsed time, and 12/24-hour clock. The dual trip-distance functions keep track of intermediate or multi-day distances. For ease of use even on rough terrain, simply pressing the bottom of the screen toggles through the computer's modes. The selected mode displays at the bottom of the screen, while current speed appears at the top in large, easy-to-read numerals. An up/down arrow compares current speed to average speed. Other features include dual tire size, programmable odometer, pace arrow, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR1620 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. The computer's tool-free bracket mounts quickly on virtually any handlebar or stem. The tool-free sensor mounts easily to the fork. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-31.8 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR1620 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye CC-RD100 Strada 8-Function Bicycle Computer Sleek, lightweight, and elegant, this slim bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed (up to 65 mph), average speed, trip distance, second-trip distance, total distance, elapsed time, and 12/24-hour clock. The dual trip-distance functions keep track of intermediate or multi-day distances. For ease of use even on rough terrain, simply pressing the bottom of the screen toggles through the computer's modes. The selected mode displays at the bottom of the screen, while current speed appears at the top in large, easy-to-read numerals. An up/down arrow compares current speed to average speed. Other features include dual tire size, programmable odometer, pace arrow, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR1620 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. The computer's tool-free bracket mounts quickly on virtually any handlebar or stem. The tool-free sensor mounts easily to the fork. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-31.8 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR1620 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41TYVpLtPvL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NRDU.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Accessories", "Electronics & Gadgets", "Cycling Computers"]]}}
{"item_id": "B000R5NREY", "title": "Cateye CC-ED300 Enduro 8-Function Bicycle Computer", "description": "Featuring a heavy-duty sensor wire suitable for off-road riding and accompanied by universal handlebar and front-fork mounts, this bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed (up to 65 mph), average speed, trip distance, second-trip distance, total distance, elapsed time, and 12/24-hour clock. The dual trip-distance functions keep track of intermediate or multi-day distances. Other features include dual tire size, programmable display, pace arrow, manual-set option for the odometer, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR2032 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-32 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR2032 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye CC-ED300 Enduro 8-Function Bicycle Computer Featuring a heavy-duty sensor wire suitable for off-road riding and accompanied by universal handlebar and front-fork mounts, this bicycle computer displays current speed, maximum speed (up to 65 mph), average speed, trip distance, second-trip distance, total distance, elapsed time, and 12/24-hour clock. The dual trip-distance functions keep track of intermediate or multi-day distances. Other features include dual tire size, programmable display, pace arrow, manual-set option for the odometer, automatic start/stop, and automatic power-saving mode. The computer runs on a CR2032 battery (included). Maximum wired transmission distance is 27 inches. Like all Cateye bicycle computers, this one is ultrasonically welded and water-resistant.Specifications:Handlebar mount size: 22-32 mmFork mount size: 11-55 mmBattery: CR2032 (included)Maximum wired transmission distance: 27\" (70 cm)About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51v%2BYn%2Bi8vL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5NREY.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "CATEYE", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Accessories", "Electronics & Gadgets", "Cycling Computers"]], "price": 75.68}}
{"item_id": "B000R5PJV8", "title": "CatEye Compact Safety Light Bicycle Rear Safety Light SL-LD100-R", "description": "These innovative lights are waterproof to 50 meters and can mount anywhere with their innovative elastric strap. A new type of magnetic switch makes it easy to turn this light on in any conditions. Three lighting modes include flashing, constant, and lternating. Available in both red and white.;", "text": "CatEye Compact Safety Light Bicycle Rear Safety Light SL-LD100-R These innovative lights are waterproof to 50 meters and can mount anywhere with their innovative elastric strap. A new type of magnetic switch makes it easy to turn this light on in any conditions. Three lighting modes include flashing, constant, and lternating. Available in both red and white.;", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41oJ2fcY3sL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5PJV8.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "CATEYE", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Lighting Parts & Accessories"]], "price": 5.99}}
{"item_id": "B000R5PJVS", "title": "Cateye TL-LD1100 LED Bicycle Tail and Safety Light (Red)", "description": "Featuring 10 red LEDs, this tail light is bright enough to be visible even during daylight and has two LEDs on each side to provide bright side visibility for extra safety. The light also incorporates Cateye's OptiCube technology, which was developed for headlights, to optimize brightness. Each row of LEDs is independently controlled by a side-mounted switch and offers four different modes, for a total of 16 combinations. Three of the modes are flashing to attract extra attention from motorists. The light mounts easily on any seat post from 18 to 44 mm in diameter. A clothing clip is also included.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "Cateye TL-LD1100 LED Bicycle Tail and Safety Light (Red) Featuring 10 red LEDs, this tail light is bright enough to be visible even during daylight and has two LEDs on each side to provide bright side visibility for extra safety. The light also incorporates Cateye's OptiCube technology, which was developed for headlights, to optimize brightness. Each row of LEDs is independently controlled by a side-mounted switch and offers four different modes, for a total of 16 combinations. Three of the modes are flashing to attract extra attention from motorists. The light mounts easily on any seat post from 18 to 44 mm in diameter. A clothing clip is also included.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41SiTYSOefL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5PJVS.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Taillights"]]}}
{"item_id": "B000R5PJX6", "title": "CatEye TL-LD150-F Bicycle Front Safety Light", "description": "Featuring five white LEDs, this tail light offers a constant mode and three flashing modes. The light mounts easily on any seat post. A clothing clip is also included. Powered by two AAA batteries, the light offers up to 90 hours of run time.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "text": "CatEye TL-LD150-F Bicycle Front Safety Light Featuring five white LEDs, this tail light offers a constant mode and three flashing modes. The light mounts easily on any seat post. A clothing clip is also included. Powered by two AAA batteries, the light offers up to 90 hours of run time.About CateyeFounded in 1946 in Osaka, Japan, CatEye is the leading manufacturer of cycle computers, lights, and reflectors to cyclists in the world. In 1964, CatEye was the first in the industry to create a flashing lamp for bicycles, followed by their first battery headlamp in 1982, and the very first bicycle head lamp using white LEDs in 2001. The company's Opticube lens and reflectors make the brightest and most efficient LED headlights. while their LD500 remains the only rear safety light that can meet the rigorous CPSC standards for reflectivity.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51gDZTovaEL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5PJX6.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Lights & Reflectors", "Taillights"]]}}
{"item_id": "B000R5PJYK", "title": "CatEye Velo 8 Bicycle Computer CC-VL810", "description": "The new Velo 8 computer is CatEye's entry-level 8 functions computer. The bracket requires no tools and is simple to use. Like the Velo 5, It features a new, larger screen and a large button for easy operation.", "text": "CatEye Velo 8 Bicycle Computer CC-VL810 The new Velo 8 computer is CatEye's entry-level 8 functions computer. The bracket requires no tools and is simple to use. Like the Velo 5, It features a new, larger screen and a large button for easy operation.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51wR-E5GxZL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B000R5PJYK.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "CATEYE", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Accessories", "Electronics & Gadgets", "Cycling Computers"]], "price": 22.25}}
