{"item_id": "B0010PR0QG", "title": "Acog 4 X 32 Scope Usmc Rifle Combat Optic For M4", "description": "Designed to the exact specifications of the United States Marine Corps, the TA31RCO-M4CP features a red dual illuminated reticle and a unique Rifle Combat Optic reticle pattern that provides quick target acquisition at close combat ranges while providing enhanced target identification and hit probability out to 800 meters. Long-range shots are delivered with greater accuracy thanks to the Bullet Drop Compensator. Coming complete with an ACOG TA51 flattop, Picatinny rail adapter mount with colt style thumbscrews, the scope is designed for use with M16M4 Weapon system (14.5-inch barrel).The TA31RCO-M4CP incorporates dual illumination technology using a combination of fiber optics and self-luminous tritium with the revolutionary, both-eyes-open Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC),for 'instinctive' target acquisition and increased hit potential. Dual illumination allows the aiming point to always be illuminated without the use of batteries. The Tritium illuminates the aiming point in total darkness, and the fiber optic self-adjusts reticle brightness during daylight according to ambient light conditions. This allows the operator to keep both eyes open while engaging targets and maintaining maximum situational awareness.The TA31RCO-M4CP scope is further distinguished by its crystal-clear and distortion-free Broad Band Anti-Reflective Coated Lens, Trijicon fiber optics and self-illuminated tritium phospor lamp for totally battery free operation, and maximum eye-relief and large exit pupil for ease of use. Constructed of military-grade aluminum alloy, the scope is dry nitrogen filled, and waterproof to 100 feet/30 meters. The scope's metal structure and optical system are backed by a lifetime warranty and the tritium lamp is guaranteed to glow for 15 years. The TA31RCO-M4CP Scope comes complete with a Scopecoat to safeguard the scope from dings and scratches, dust, dirt, and moisture in the field and a Lenspen that makes it safe and easy to clean the scope's lens in the field.Features:Trijicon Fiber Optics: Automatically adjusts the brightness level and contrast of the reticle to available light conditions.Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC): Trijicon ACOG models equipped with BAC allow use of the both-eyes-open aiming method along with scope magnification sighting for rapid target acquisition--in any light.Broad Band Anti-Reflective Coated Lenses: Multi-coated lenses provide superior clarity and light gathering capabilities with zero distortion.Trijicon Tritium Phospor Lamp: Aiming reticle glows in low-light conditions for quick target acquisition--with no batteries to fail. Lamp is guaranteed to illuminate for up to 15 years.Internally Adjustable: Since only the prism housing moves, the ACOG is much more rugged than conventional designs.Longer Eye-Relief: Maximum eye-relief for larger caliber rifles and large exit pupil for faster target acquisition.Military-Grade Aluminum Alloy Housing: Forged 7075-T6 aircraft aluminum alloy housing provides for a nearly indestructible sighting system.Waterproof to 100 Feet/30 Meters: Dry nitrogen filled to eliminate fogging.Totally Battery Free: Trijicon ACOG delivers increased hit potential in all lighting conditions--without the use of failure-prone batteries.Specifications:Magnification: 4XObjective Size: 32 millimetersBullet Drop Compensator: YesLength: 5.8 inchesWeight: 9.9 ouncesIllumination source: Fiber Optics and TritiumReticle Pattern: Chevron with Target Reference SystemDay/Night Reticle Color: RedCalibration: 0.223Bindon Aiming Concept: YesEye Relief: 1.5 inchesExit Pupil: 8 millimetersField of View: 7 degreesField of View @ 100 yards: 36.8 feetAdjustment @ 100 yards: 3 clicks per inchMount: TA51 (included)Mount on: FlattopHousing Material: forged aluminumWater-resistant to 100 feetWhat's in the Box?TA31RCO-M4CP Combat Optic (RCO) with Red Dual Illuminated Reticle riflescope, TA51 Mount), ACOG Thumb Screw (RCO) (TA53A), RCO 4x32 ACOG Pouch (TA86), 4x32 RCO killFLASH, Adjuster Cap Lanyards, 4x32 Scopecoat, Lenspen, Trijicon Logo Sticker, RCO Manual, warranty cardManufacturer WarrantyLimited Lifetime: optical systems and metal structure; 15-years: Tritium lampAbout ACOG (Advanced Combat Optical Gunsight) Riflescopes:Trijicon ACOG riflescopes are internally adjustable, compact telescopic sights with tritium illuminated reticle patterns for use in low light or at night. The ACOG's combine traditional, precise distance marksmanship with close-in aiming speed. Designed for use with the M16 family, every feature of the ACOG's mechanical and optical design was chosen for a single purpose: to provide increased hit potential in all lighting conditions--without failure-prone batteries.With a dual-illuminated reticle, the Trijicon ACOG provides shooters with a distinct aiming point in all light conditions--without batteries. Powered by a tritium-phosphor lamp, the gunsight's reticle glows in low-light conditions, while advanced fiber optics automatically adjust the brightness level and contrast of the reticle in brighter light conditions. Broadband, anti-reflective coated lenses provide superior clarity and light gathering capabilities with zero distortion. The ACOG also offers large eye volume, giving you greater leeway--fore and aft, and from side to side--with which to see through the lens. Of course, once the target is acquired, the ACOG is a trusted ally to help you zero in on a perfect shot.The ACOG is crafted with a tough, military-grade, aluminum-alloy housing and is waterproof to depths of 500 feet--making it nearly indestructible. Only the prism housing moves, so it's much more rugged than conventional designs. And the ACOG does not require failure-prone batteries--so you can rely on it to perform in practically every situation.Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC):Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC) ACOG Riflescopes feature bright daytime reticles using fiber optics, which collect ambient light. This revolutionary, both-eyes-open aiming method provides you with 'instinctive' target acquisition and increased hit potential. And, the scope's ranging is built into many of its reticles, so you only need to set zero once for a multitude of ranging distances.ACOG Scopecoat:The Scopecoat is constructed of the highest quality neoprene laminated with nylon. Its simple design safeguards the scope or sighting system from dings and scratches, dust, dirt, and moisture. Neoprene has 5 percent greater moisture absorbency, which takes moisture (condensation and sweating) away from the scope or sight and helps protect it from rust and corrosion. The nylon laminate shields the scope against the elements. Simply stretch both ends of the Scopecoat over your ACOG sight for optimum field protection.Lenspen:The Lenspen features a safe and easy to use retractable dust removal brush and a special non-liquid cleaning element, designed to never dry out.", "text": "Acog 4 X 32 Scope Usmc Rifle Combat Optic For M4 Designed to the exact specifications of the United States Marine Corps, the TA31RCO-M4CP features a red dual illuminated reticle and a unique Rifle Combat Optic reticle pattern that provides quick target acquisition at close combat ranges while providing enhanced target identification and hit probability out to 800 meters. Long-range shots are delivered with greater accuracy thanks to the Bullet Drop Compensator. Coming complete with an ACOG TA51 flattop, Picatinny rail adapter mount with colt style thumbscrews, the scope is designed for use with M16M4 Weapon system (14.5-inch barrel).The TA31RCO-M4CP incorporates dual illumination technology using a combination of fiber optics and self-luminous tritium with the revolutionary, both-eyes-open Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC),for 'instinctive' target acquisition and increased hit potential. Dual illumination allows the aiming point to always be illuminated without the use of batteries. The Tritium illuminates the aiming point in total darkness, and the fiber optic self-adjusts reticle brightness during daylight according to ambient light conditions. This allows the operator to keep both eyes open while engaging targets and maintaining maximum situational awareness.The TA31RCO-M4CP scope is further distinguished by its crystal-clear and distortion-free Broad Band Anti-Reflective Coated Lens, Trijicon fiber optics and self-illuminated tritium phospor lamp for totally battery free operation, and maximum eye-relief and large exit pupil for ease of use. Constructed of military-grade aluminum alloy, the scope is dry nitrogen filled, and waterproof to 100 feet/30 meters. The scope's metal structure and optical system are backed by a lifetime warranty and the tritium lamp is guaranteed to glow for 15 years. The TA31RCO-M4CP Scope comes complete with a Scopecoat to safeguard the scope from dings and scratches, dust, dirt, and moisture in the field and a Lenspen that makes it safe and easy to clean the scope's lens in the field.Features:Trijicon Fiber Optics: Automatically adjusts the brightness level and contrast of the reticle to available light conditions.Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC): Trijicon ACOG models equipped with BAC allow use of the both-eyes-open aiming method along with scope magnification sighting for rapid target acquisition--in any light.Broad Band Anti-Reflective Coated Lenses: Multi-coated lenses provide superior clarity and light gathering capabilities with zero distortion.Trijicon Tritium Phospor Lamp: Aiming reticle glows in low-light conditions for quick target acquisition--with no batteries to fail. Lamp is guaranteed to illuminate for up to 15 years.Internally Adjustable: Since only the prism housing moves, the ACOG is much more rugged than conventional designs.Longer Eye-Relief: Maximum eye-relief for larger caliber rifles and large exit pupil for faster target acquisition.Military-Grade Aluminum Alloy Housing: Forged 7075-T6 aircraft aluminum alloy housing provides for a nearly indestructible sighting system.Waterproof to 100 Feet/30 Meters: Dry nitrogen filled to eliminate fogging.Totally Battery Free: Trijicon ACOG delivers increased hit potential in all lighting conditions--without the use of failure-prone batteries.Specifications:Magnification: 4XObjective Size: 32 millimetersBullet Drop Compensator: YesLength: 5.8 inchesWeight: 9.9 ouncesIllumination source: Fiber Optics and TritiumReticle Pattern: Chevron with Target Reference SystemDay/Night Reticle Color: RedCalibration: 0.223Bindon Aiming Concept: YesEye Relief: 1.5 inchesExit Pupil: 8 millimetersField of View: 7 degreesField of View @ 100 yards: 36.8 feetAdjustment @ 100 yards: 3 clicks per inchMount: TA51 (included)Mount on: FlattopHousing Material: forged aluminumWater-resistant to 100 feetWhat's in the Box?TA31RCO-M4CP Combat Optic (RCO) with Red Dual Illuminated Reticle riflescope, TA51 Mount), ACOG Thumb Screw (RCO) (TA53A), RCO 4x32 ACOG Pouch (TA86), 4x32 RCO killFLASH, Adjuster Cap Lanyards, 4x32 Scopecoat, Lenspen, Trijicon Logo Sticker, RCO Manual, warranty cardManufacturer WarrantyLimited Lifetime: optical systems and metal structure; 15-years: Tritium lampAbout ACOG (Advanced Combat Optical Gunsight) Riflescopes:Trijicon ACOG riflescopes are internally adjustable, compact telescopic sights with tritium illuminated reticle patterns for use in low light or at night. The ACOG's combine traditional, precise distance marksmanship with close-in aiming speed. Designed for use with the M16 family, every feature of the ACOG's mechanical and optical design was chosen for a single purpose: to provide increased hit potential in all lighting conditions--without failure-prone batteries.With a dual-illuminated reticle, the Trijicon ACOG provides shooters with a distinct aiming point in all light conditions--without batteries. Powered by a tritium-phosphor lamp, the gunsight's reticle glows in low-light conditions, while advanced fiber optics automatically adjust the brightness level and contrast of the reticle in brighter light conditions. Broadband, anti-reflective coated lenses provide superior clarity and light gathering capabilities with zero distortion. The ACOG also offers large eye volume, giving you greater leeway--fore and aft, and from side to side--with which to see through the lens. Of course, once the target is acquired, the ACOG is a trusted ally to help you zero in on a perfect shot.The ACOG is crafted with a tough, military-grade, aluminum-alloy housing and is waterproof to depths of 500 feet--making it nearly indestructible. Only the prism housing moves, so it's much more rugged than conventional designs. And the ACOG does not require failure-prone batteries--so you can rely on it to perform in practically every situation.Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC):Bindon Aiming Concept (BAC) ACOG Riflescopes feature bright daytime reticles using fiber optics, which collect ambient light. This revolutionary, both-eyes-open aiming method provides you with 'instinctive' target acquisition and increased hit potential. And, the scope's ranging is built into many of its reticles, so you only need to set zero once for a multitude of ranging distances.ACOG Scopecoat:The Scopecoat is constructed of the highest quality neoprene laminated with nylon. Its simple design safeguards the scope or sighting system from dings and scratches, dust, dirt, and moisture. Neoprene has 5 percent greater moisture absorbency, which takes moisture (condensation and sweating) away from the scope or sight and helps protect it from rust and corrosion. The nylon laminate shields the scope against the elements. Simply stretch both ends of the Scopecoat over your ACOG sight for optimum field protection.Lenspen:The Lenspen features a safe and easy to use retractable dust removal brush and a special non-liquid cleaning element, designed to never dry out.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/313Sx5sE7QL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0010PR0QG.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "ACOG", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Spotting Scopes"]]}}
