{"item_id": "B0016WOEZ8", "title": "Aimpoint 2OA CompM3 Sight", "description": "This professional-grade sight is frequently used by law enforcement officers, soldiers, and those who demand the most from their weaponry.When police and armed forces personnel are on duty, they need their equipment to handle just about any situation, anytime, anywhere. With this in mind, Aimpoint created the CompM3, an innovative sight that offers the highest standard available for sight systems technology. Advanced Circuit Efficiency Technology (ACET) provides battery life of up to five years, and the CompM3 is compatible with any generation of Aimpoint's night vision devices.The CompM3 features Aimpoint's latest technology, and is even more rugged than most of the company's legendarily durable tactical gear. It comes with a replaceable outer black rubber cover, which protects it from scratching while improving stealth. The unit is unaffected by extreme weather conditions and is submersible in up to 150 feet of water.FeaturesUnlimited field of view and optimal light transmissionParallax-free with unlimited eye reliefNo harmful laser emissionsMechanical switch for speed and reliabilityACET technology allows 50,000 hours of operation on single battery500,000 hours of use on NVD settingAvailable in two- and four-dot sizesSubmersible to 150 feetComes with replaceable outer black rubber coverOptical Data:LED light source650nm red lightAnti-reflex coating on all surfaces and multi-layer coating objective lens1X magnificationElectronic Data:Runs on one three-volt lithium battery (type 2L76 or DL1/3N)Approximately 50,000 hours of battery life, or five years of continuous use500,000 hours of battery life at NVD settingsManual rotary switch dot intensity adjustmentSix DL daylight settingsFour NVD settingsMechanical Data:High strength extruded aluminum housingHard anodized matte finishOne-click adjustment; 0.5-inch at 100 yardsOne ring, 30-millimeter mountingEnvironmental Data:-50 to 160 degrees Fahrenheit operating temperature rangeSubmersible to 150 feetDimensions:Sight measures 2.2 by 2.2 by 5.1 inches (W x H x D)38-millimeter objective diameter30-millimeter tube diameter7.8-ounce sight weight1.7-ounce rubber cover weightWarrantyAimpoint products include limited manufacturer's warranties of two years for professional or competitive use, and ten years for personal or recreational use.About AimpointIn 1974, a small group of Swedish entrepreneurs started exploring ways to improve shooting accuracy, with the deceptively simple goal of creating a sighting technology that would allow shooters to acquire their target quickly, and hit moving targets in all weather and lighting conditions consistently and accurately. The result of their efforts, the now ubiquitous red dot sight, would eventually revolutionize the shooting and hunting industry.The company's first commercial sight product, the Aimpoint Electronic, was introduced in 1975, and quickly developed a reputation as one of the fastest way to aim a firearm. The Aimpoint red dot sight has continued to evolve over the past 35 years by working closely with experienced hunters, marksmen and military weapon experts, and there are more than one million Aimpoint red dot sights in use worldwide today.", "text": "Aimpoint 2OA CompM3 Sight This professional-grade sight is frequently used by law enforcement officers, soldiers, and those who demand the most from their weaponry.When police and armed forces personnel are on duty, they need their equipment to handle just about any situation, anytime, anywhere. With this in mind, Aimpoint created the CompM3, an innovative sight that offers the highest standard available for sight systems technology. Advanced Circuit Efficiency Technology (ACET) provides battery life of up to five years, and the CompM3 is compatible with any generation of Aimpoint's night vision devices.The CompM3 features Aimpoint's latest technology, and is even more rugged than most of the company's legendarily durable tactical gear. It comes with a replaceable outer black rubber cover, which protects it from scratching while improving stealth. The unit is unaffected by extreme weather conditions and is submersible in up to 150 feet of water.FeaturesUnlimited field of view and optimal light transmissionParallax-free with unlimited eye reliefNo harmful laser emissionsMechanical switch for speed and reliabilityACET technology allows 50,000 hours of operation on single battery500,000 hours of use on NVD settingAvailable in two- and four-dot sizesSubmersible to 150 feetComes with replaceable outer black rubber coverOptical Data:LED light source650nm red lightAnti-reflex coating on all surfaces and multi-layer coating objective lens1X magnificationElectronic Data:Runs on one three-volt lithium battery (type 2L76 or DL1/3N)Approximately 50,000 hours of battery life, or five years of continuous use500,000 hours of battery life at NVD settingsManual rotary switch dot intensity adjustmentSix DL daylight settingsFour NVD settingsMechanical Data:High strength extruded aluminum housingHard anodized matte finishOne-click adjustment; 0.5-inch at 100 yardsOne ring, 30-millimeter mountingEnvironmental Data:-50 to 160 degrees Fahrenheit operating temperature rangeSubmersible to 150 feetDimensions:Sight measures 2.2 by 2.2 by 5.1 inches (W x H x D)38-millimeter objective diameter30-millimeter tube diameter7.8-ounce sight weight1.7-ounce rubber cover weightWarrantyAimpoint products include limited manufacturer's warranties of two years for professional or competitive use, and ten years for personal or recreational use.About AimpointIn 1974, a small group of Swedish entrepreneurs started exploring ways to improve shooting accuracy, with the deceptively simple goal of creating a sighting technology that would allow shooters to acquire their target quickly, and hit moving targets in all weather and lighting conditions consistently and accurately. The result of their efforts, the now ubiquitous red dot sight, would eventually revolutionize the shooting and hunting industry.The company's first commercial sight product, the Aimpoint Electronic, was introduced in 1975, and quickly developed a reputation as one of the fastest way to aim a firearm. The Aimpoint red dot sight has continued to evolve over the past 35 years by working closely with experienced hunters, marksmen and military weapon experts, and there are more than one million Aimpoint red dot sights in use worldwide today.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41RlxW5ZJWL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0016WOEZ8.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "AimPoint", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Night Vision"]], "price": 576.99}}
{"item_id": "B0016WVQJU", "title": "SABRE FRONTIERSMAN Bear Attack Deterrent", "description": "Nothing ruins a good hike as fast as a large, menacing bear. Now you can protect yourself on hikes wherever you go with this Frontiersman bear attack deterrent, which is proven effective against grizzlies, brown and black bears, and a variety of other large mammals. Available in 7.9- and 9.2-ounce sizes, Frontiersman deterrent boasts a range of 35 feet--up to 3 feet further than other bear sprays. This is a huge advantage when hiking, as charging bears can cover more than 30 feet per second. To use, simply spray the dual-propellant system in the direction of the bear. Each one-second blast of Frontiersman contains up to 84 percent more spray than other brands, putting a large barrier between you and the charging bear. Within five seconds, the can will be empty and you'll be protected by a heavy fog of oleoresin capsicum--a natural, resin-like substance derived from hot peppers. The substance will cause an immediate but temporary burning sensation on the bear's skin and eyes, giving you time to scamper away. Frontiersman bear repellant is effective both day and night, with a glow-in-the-dark safety wedge that prevents accidental discharge after the sun goes down. Plus, should an uninvited 800-pound guest come knocking at the door of your tent or RV, the glow-in-the-dark wedge will help you quickly locate your Frontiersman canister. Hikers can protect themselves even further by purchasing one of Sabre's unique holsters (sold separately), which allow immediate access to the firing mechanism. The hip belt holster makes it easy to fire the canister from the hip, while the chest holster puts the canister right in front of you. No bear spray is hotter than Frontiersman, yet the spray is completely safe for bears, causing only temporary burning and discomfort. (The EPA sets strict limits on the amount of heat-bearing chemicals used in bear repellent sprays.) And the Frontiersman has been field tested in some of the most challenging environments in North America, including the Elmendorf Air Force Base in Elmendorf, Alaska, and Brown Bear Resources in Missoula, Montana.", "text": "SABRE FRONTIERSMAN Bear Attack Deterrent Nothing ruins a good hike as fast as a large, menacing bear. Now you can protect yourself on hikes wherever you go with this Frontiersman bear attack deterrent, which is proven effective against grizzlies, brown and black bears, and a variety of other large mammals. Available in 7.9- and 9.2-ounce sizes, Frontiersman deterrent boasts a range of 35 feet--up to 3 feet further than other bear sprays. This is a huge advantage when hiking, as charging bears can cover more than 30 feet per second. To use, simply spray the dual-propellant system in the direction of the bear. Each one-second blast of Frontiersman contains up to 84 percent more spray than other brands, putting a large barrier between you and the charging bear. Within five seconds, the can will be empty and you'll be protected by a heavy fog of oleoresin capsicum--a natural, resin-like substance derived from hot peppers. The substance will cause an immediate but temporary burning sensation on the bear's skin and eyes, giving you time to scamper away. Frontiersman bear repellant is effective both day and night, with a glow-in-the-dark safety wedge that prevents accidental discharge after the sun goes down. Plus, should an uninvited 800-pound guest come knocking at the door of your tent or RV, the glow-in-the-dark wedge will help you quickly locate your Frontiersman canister. Hikers can protect themselves even further by purchasing one of Sabre's unique holsters (sold separately), which allow immediate access to the firing mechanism. The hip belt holster makes it easy to fire the canister from the hip, while the chest holster puts the canister right in front of you. No bear spray is hotter than Frontiersman, yet the spray is completely safe for bears, causing only temporary burning and discomfort. (The EPA sets strict limits on the amount of heat-bearing chemicals used in bear repellent sprays.) And the Frontiersman has been field tested in some of the most challenging environments in North America, including the Elmendorf Air Force Base in Elmendorf, Alaska, and Brown Bear Resources in Missoula, Montana.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/4169jjJ28uL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0016WVQJU.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Outdoor Gear", "Camping & Hiking", "Safety & Survival", "Bear Protection"]]}}
