{"item_id": "B0017CV9FK", "title": "Signal Mirror - 2\"x 3\" Pouch - Olive Drab", "description": "OLive Drab Signal Mirror Pouch: Padded, Pouch Made of 1000 Denier Nylon", "text": "Signal Mirror - 2\"x 3\" Pouch - Olive Drab OLive Drab Signal Mirror Pouch: Padded, Pouch Made of 1000 Denier Nylon", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31YH-I4DLpL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0017CV9FK.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors"]], "price": 5.0}}
{"item_id": "B0017DE16I", "title": "Sting Ray - Front Squat Stabilizer", "description": "Sting Ray Front Squat Support Harness Use this to take the stress and painful weight off of your shoulders when doing front squats Sting Ray Front Squat Support Harness The Front Squat is a great exercise for the athlete, bodybuilder, powerlifter, or for people with general fitness goals, but the negative aspects of the movement bring a ton of excess baggage. Most strength coaches prefer the Olympic clean style grip because it gives the lifter a wider \"rack\" on the bar and therefore more stability. The problem with this conventional grip is that it's almost impossible for anyone with shoulder, elbow or wrist problems and most lifters lack the necessary flexibility in these joints anyway. This grip also requires external rotation of the Humerus (upper arm bone) stressing the shoulder joint and mechanically causing even more limits on flexibility. The crossed arm grip has a load of downsides too. Narrow rack with less stability, more crush to the shoulders and it's harder to keep the bar from rolling back into the throat, or down the arms. No wonder the front squat is usually tried once and tossed out. With either grip the bar can rest on the collar bone, press down on the sternum and cause the lifter to run out of breath long before leg strength. Now, the Sting Ray? removes all these negatives from one of the most powerful exercises available. The Sting Ray?: Lifts the bar off the collar bone allowing full expansion of the rib cage! Provides easy bar control without stressing shoulder, elbow, or wrists! Allows the widest rack on the body by moving the load out to the front delt! Keeps the Humerus in a safe neutral position! Protects the lifters body so all new repair tissue goes where you want it! Small and lightweight yet virtually indestructible for years of tough service!", "text": "Sting Ray - Front Squat Stabilizer Sting Ray Front Squat Support Harness Use this to take the stress and painful weight off of your shoulders when doing front squats Sting Ray Front Squat Support Harness The Front Squat is a great exercise for the athlete, bodybuilder, powerlifter, or for people with general fitness goals, but the negative aspects of the movement bring a ton of excess baggage. Most strength coaches prefer the Olympic clean style grip because it gives the lifter a wider \"rack\" on the bar and therefore more stability. The problem with this conventional grip is that it's almost impossible for anyone with shoulder, elbow or wrist problems and most lifters lack the necessary flexibility in these joints anyway. This grip also requires external rotation of the Humerus (upper arm bone) stressing the shoulder joint and mechanically causing even more limits on flexibility. The crossed arm grip has a load of downsides too. Narrow rack with less stability, more crush to the shoulders and it's harder to keep the bar from rolling back into the throat, or down the arms. No wonder the front squat is usually tried once and tossed out. With either grip the bar can rest on the collar bone, press down on the sternum and cause the lifter to run out of breath long before leg strength. Now, the Sting Ray? removes all these negatives from one of the most powerful exercises available. The Sting Ray?: Lifts the bar off the collar bone allowing full expansion of the rib cage! Provides easy bar control without stressing shoulder, elbow, or wrists! Allows the widest rack on the body by moving the load out to the front delt! Keeps the Humerus in a safe neutral position! Protects the lifters body so all new repair tissue goes where you want it! Small and lightweight yet virtually indestructible for years of tough service!", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41fKVe1KosL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0017DE16I.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Sting Ray", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Exercise & Fitness", "Strength Training Equipment", "Leg Machines"]], "price": 39.45}}
{"item_id": "B0017DEJ1U", "title": "Crosman 764SB air rifle", "description": "", "text": "Crosman 764SB air rifle", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/214sRj0j%2BXL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0017DEJ1U.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Crosman", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Airsoft, Air Guns & Slingshots", "Air Guns", "Air Rifles"]], "price": 39.95}}
{"item_id": "B0017DGBY8", "title": "Manta Ray", "description": "Maintain an upright position when performing back squats. Load distribution principle transfers weight across trapezius muscles, reducing neck pain and discomfort.", "text": "Manta Ray Maintain an upright position when performing back squats. Load distribution principle transfers weight across trapezius muscles, reducing neck pain and discomfort.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31Awoa13XTL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0017DGBY8.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Advance Fitness, Inc.", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Exercise & Fitness", "Accessories", "Collars"]], "price": 44.95}}
{"item_id": "B0017DGLJI", "title": "Aimpoint H-1 4 MOA Micro Sight", "description": "On a bow, the parallax-free H-1 Micro eliminates the need for a peep, allowing you to shoot accurately in lower light.With the Micro H-1, Aimpoint has introduced an aiming system that provides the performance of full-sized sights in the smallest package possible. Designed with the hunter in mind, this sight can be used on any type of firearm or archery equipment, including rifles, bows, hunting revolvers, and bows. The compact, lightweight sight weighs less than four ounces including the integrated mount, and can be easily piggybacked on top of larger magnifying scopes optics. Aimpoint's unique band-pass coating on the front lens provides optimal dot brightness, as well as clear, crisp images.FeaturesParallax-free with unlimited field of view and eye reliefRugged, durable construction, unaffected by extreme conditionsNo harmful laser emissionsMechanical switch for speed and reliabilityLightweight at only 84 grams without mount and 105 grams withIntegral Weaver-style base allows easy attachmentACET technology allows 50,000 hours of operation on one batteryAvailable in four MOA (minutes of angle)Patent pending mount is keyed to the sight body to absorb recoilPrecision adjustment for windage and elevationTop of protective caps fits into holes on adjustment screws; no other tool required12 settings for use in daylight and low light conditionsOptical Data:LED light source650nm red lightAnti-reflex coating on all surfaces and multi-layer coating objective lens1X magnificationElectronic Data:Runs on one three-volt lithium battery (type CR2032)Approximately 50,000 hours of battery life, or five years of continuous useManual rotary switch dot intensity adjustment12 DL daylight settingsMechanical Data:High strength extruded aluminum housingHard anodized matte finishOne-click adjustment; 0.5-inch at 100 yardsIntegrated Picatinny/Weaver mountingEnvironmental Data:-20 to 140 degrees Fahrenheit operating temperature rangeFully waterproofDimensions:Sight measures 1.6 by 1.4 by 2.4 inches (W x H x D)Measures 2.4 by 1.6 by 2.4 inches (W x H x D) with mountSight weighs three ouncesWeighs 3.7 ounces with integrated mountWarrantyAimpoint products include limited manufacturer's warranties of two years for professional or competitive use, and ten years for personal or recreational use.About AimpointIn 1974, a small group of Swedish entrepreneurs started exploring ways to improve shooting accuracy, with the deceptively simple goal of creating a sighting technology that would allow shooters to acquire their target quickly, and hit moving targets in all weather and lighting conditions consistently and accurately. The result of their efforts, the now ubiquitous red dot sight, would eventually revolutionize the shooting and hunting industry.The company's first commercial sight product, the Aimpoint Electronic, was introduced in 1975, and quickly developed a reputation as one of the fastest way to aim a firearm. The Aimpoint red dot sight has continued to evolve over the past 35 years by working closely with experienced hunters, marksmen and military weapon experts, and there are more than one million Aimpoint red dot sights in use worldwide today.", "text": "Aimpoint H-1 4 MOA Micro Sight On a bow, the parallax-free H-1 Micro eliminates the need for a peep, allowing you to shoot accurately in lower light.With the Micro H-1, Aimpoint has introduced an aiming system that provides the performance of full-sized sights in the smallest package possible. Designed with the hunter in mind, this sight can be used on any type of firearm or archery equipment, including rifles, bows, hunting revolvers, and bows. The compact, lightweight sight weighs less than four ounces including the integrated mount, and can be easily piggybacked on top of larger magnifying scopes optics. Aimpoint's unique band-pass coating on the front lens provides optimal dot brightness, as well as clear, crisp images.FeaturesParallax-free with unlimited field of view and eye reliefRugged, durable construction, unaffected by extreme conditionsNo harmful laser emissionsMechanical switch for speed and reliabilityLightweight at only 84 grams without mount and 105 grams withIntegral Weaver-style base allows easy attachmentACET technology allows 50,000 hours of operation on one batteryAvailable in four MOA (minutes of angle)Patent pending mount is keyed to the sight body to absorb recoilPrecision adjustment for windage and elevationTop of protective caps fits into holes on adjustment screws; no other tool required12 settings for use in daylight and low light conditionsOptical Data:LED light source650nm red lightAnti-reflex coating on all surfaces and multi-layer coating objective lens1X magnificationElectronic Data:Runs on one three-volt lithium battery (type CR2032)Approximately 50,000 hours of battery life, or five years of continuous useManual rotary switch dot intensity adjustment12 DL daylight settingsMechanical Data:High strength extruded aluminum housingHard anodized matte finishOne-click adjustment; 0.5-inch at 100 yardsIntegrated Picatinny/Weaver mountingEnvironmental Data:-20 to 140 degrees Fahrenheit operating temperature rangeFully waterproofDimensions:Sight measures 1.6 by 1.4 by 2.4 inches (W x H x D)Measures 2.4 by 1.6 by 2.4 inches (W x H x D) with mountSight weighs three ouncesWeighs 3.7 ounces with integrated mountWarrantyAimpoint products include limited manufacturer's warranties of two years for professional or competitive use, and ten years for personal or recreational use.About AimpointIn 1974, a small group of Swedish entrepreneurs started exploring ways to improve shooting accuracy, with the deceptively simple goal of creating a sighting technology that would allow shooters to acquire their target quickly, and hit moving targets in all weather and lighting conditions consistently and accurately. The result of their efforts, the now ubiquitous red dot sight, would eventually revolutionize the shooting and hunting industry.The company's first commercial sight product, the Aimpoint Electronic, was introduced in 1975, and quickly developed a reputation as one of the fastest way to aim a firearm. The Aimpoint red dot sight has continued to evolve over the past 35 years by working closely with experienced hunters, marksmen and military weapon experts, and there are more than one million Aimpoint red dot sights in use worldwide today.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41m101n3oEL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B0017DGLJI.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "AimPoint", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 583.01}}
