{"item_id": "B001HN5GB2", "title": "Leupold Alumina Flip Back Lens Cover Standard Ep 59055", "description": "Leupold optics have long set the standard for high performance, and now, with Alumina accessories, the company sets the standard for adaptability, too. Each Alumina flip-back lens cover features a powerful neodymium magnet to hold it securely closed over the lens, along with triple O-ring seals for maximum protection from the elements. More significantly, the cover flips open easily when you want to view an object through your Leupold riflescope, so you don't need to manually remove the cover before targeting an object. The cover is even clockable, so you can rotate it to open in any direction. Other details include a machined-aluminum precision construction, a low-profile design, and quick and easy operation. This particular matte black cover is designed for Leupold Standard EP lenses, but covers are available for a variety of other sizes of eyepieces and objective lenses.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Alumina Flip Back Lens Cover Standard Ep 59055 Leupold optics have long set the standard for high performance, and now, with Alumina accessories, the company sets the standard for adaptability, too. Each Alumina flip-back lens cover features a powerful neodymium magnet to hold it securely closed over the lens, along with triple O-ring seals for maximum protection from the elements. More significantly, the cover flips open easily when you want to view an object through your Leupold riflescope, so you don't need to manually remove the cover before targeting an object. The cover is even clockable, so you can rotate it to open in any direction. Other details include a machined-aluminum precision construction, a low-profile design, and quick and easy operation. This particular matte black cover is designed for Leupold Standard EP lenses, but covers are available for a variety of other sizes of eyepieces and objective lenses.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41XKTN5fQ4L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GB2.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 49.0}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5GCG", "title": "Leupold Alumina Flip Back Lens Cover Kit-40Mm And Standard Ep 62990", "description": "Alumina® flip-back lens covers – feature powerful neodymium magnets to hold them securely closed and triple O-ring seals for maximum protection from the elements. Their machined-aluminum precision construction, quick and easy operation, and a low-profile position when open make our flip-back lens covers stand above the rest. The round objective models are clockable, so you can rotate them to open any direction. Available in a variety of sizes for both eyepieces and objectives.", "text": "Leupold Alumina Flip Back Lens Cover Kit-40Mm And Standard Ep 62990 Alumina® flip-back lens covers – feature powerful neodymium magnets to hold them securely closed and triple O-ring seals for maximum protection from the elements. Their machined-aluminum precision construction, quick and easy operation, and a low-profile position when open make our flip-back lens covers stand above the rest. The round objective models are clockable, so you can rotate them to open any direction. Available in a variety of sizes for both eyepieces and objectives.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41DX%2BHsWCiL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GCG.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics"]], "price": 89.05}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5GK8", "title": "Leupold Zero Point Boresighter 59012", "description": "This Leupold Zero Point Boresighter features a unique lens aperture system that eliminates point of aim errors resulting from parallax due to extreme misalignment. The boresighter also includes natural backlighting of the target, LED illumination for use in low-light settings, and an inch scale for measuring approximate riflescope height and target group sizes. Check your zero. Set new ranges. It's compatible with any caliber firearm. The energy efficient design yields 25 hours of battery life. Range cards for recording sight-in information are included.", "text": "Leupold Zero Point Boresighter 59012 This Leupold Zero Point Boresighter features a unique lens aperture system that eliminates point of aim errors resulting from parallax due to extreme misalignment. The boresighter also includes natural backlighting of the target, LED illumination for use in low-light settings, and an inch scale for measuring approximate riflescope height and target group sizes. Check your zero. Set new ranges. It's compatible with any caliber firearm. The energy efficient design yields 25 hours of battery life. Range cards for recording sight-in information are included.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41ZUZGydgsL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GK8.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Boresighters"]]}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5GQM", "title": "Leupold 4\"\"-40Mm Lens Shade Matte (Post 2004) 56190", "description": "Leupold optics have long set the standard for high performance, and now, with Alumina accessories, the company sets the standard for adaptability, too. This four-inch lens shade, for example, fits all 2004 and newer VX-II, VX-III, and Mark 4 40mm objective scopes. In addition, users can thread together multiple 2.5-inch or four-inch shades to create custom lengths. The matte black shade is also available in other sizes, such as 45mm and 50mm.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold 4\"\"-40Mm Lens Shade Matte (Post 2004) 56190 Leupold optics have long set the standard for high performance, and now, with Alumina accessories, the company sets the standard for adaptability, too. This four-inch lens shade, for example, fits all 2004 and newer VX-II, VX-III, and Mark 4 40mm objective scopes. In addition, users can thread together multiple 2.5-inch or four-inch shades to create custom lengths. The matte black shade is also available in other sizes, such as 45mm and 50mm.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31I7UyX9I6L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GQM.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 52.99}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5GS0", "title": "Leupold Quick Release Binocular Harness 55895", "description": "Even the lightest binoculars can get heavy after hours of hanging around your neck. Now, with the quick release binocular harness, the weight is taken off your neck and evenly distributed across your back through the “X”-shaped design of the strap, keeping your binoculars close to your body to prevent swinging yet ready at a moment’s notice.", "text": "Leupold Quick Release Binocular Harness 55895 Even the lightest binoculars can get heavy after hours of hanging around your neck. Now, with the quick release binocular harness, the weight is taken off your neck and evenly distributed across your back through the “X”-shaped design of the strap, keeping your binoculars close to your body to prevent swinging yet ready at a moment’s notice.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/410w99kJA5L._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GS0.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics"]], "price": 24.39}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5GXK", "title": "Leupold Scope Cover Medium 53574", "description": "The right tool makes even the most difficult or tedious job easier. Enter the medium Leupold scope cover, which will keep your Leupold scope looking like new. Available in many sizes to fit most Leupold scopes, the cover is made of water-resistant, nylon-laminated neoprene. Once on, the cover protects your scope from dirt and damage whether in storage or in the field.The medium scope cover fits the following scope models:VX-II 2-7x28mm UltralightVX-II 3-9x33mm UltralightVX-II 3-9x33mm Ultralight EFR and Rimfire EFRVX-I 2-7x28mm Ultralight RimfireFX-II 4x28mm HandgunVX-III 2.5-8x32mm HandgunVX-7 2.5-10x45mmVX-III 1.75-6x32mmVX-III 2.5-8x36mmVX-II 2-7x33mmVX-I 2-7x33mm (and Shotgun/Muzzleloader, NWTF Edition)Rifleman 2-7x33mm (and Shotgun/Muzzleloader)FX-II 2.5x28mm IER ScoutFX-II 4x33mmFX-II 6x36mmAbout LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Scope Cover Medium 53574 The right tool makes even the most difficult or tedious job easier. Enter the medium Leupold scope cover, which will keep your Leupold scope looking like new. Available in many sizes to fit most Leupold scopes, the cover is made of water-resistant, nylon-laminated neoprene. Once on, the cover protects your scope from dirt and damage whether in storage or in the field.The medium scope cover fits the following scope models:VX-II 2-7x28mm UltralightVX-II 3-9x33mm UltralightVX-II 3-9x33mm Ultralight EFR and Rimfire EFRVX-I 2-7x28mm Ultralight RimfireFX-II 4x28mm HandgunVX-III 2.5-8x32mm HandgunVX-7 2.5-10x45mmVX-III 1.75-6x32mmVX-III 2.5-8x36mmVX-II 2-7x33mmVX-I 2-7x33mm (and Shotgun/Muzzleloader, NWTF Edition)Rifleman 2-7x33mm (and Shotgun/Muzzleloader)FX-II 2.5x28mm IER ScoutFX-II 4x33mmFX-II 6x36mmAbout LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31V0mJeRD2L._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5GXK.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 19.51}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5H4S", "title": "Leupold Lens Pen 48807", "description": "The right tool makes even the most difficult or tedious job easier. Enter the compact, two-step Leupold LensPen, which will keep your riflescope and binocular lenses clean and pristine. The LensPen offers a natural hairbrush that's fully retractable when not in use (a clean brush is key because it's the first thing to touch the lens), along with a microfiber cleaning tip that automatically replenishes itself with a state-of-the-art cleaning compound. Overall, the LensPen is far easier and more effective than other lens cleaning methods. Compact and ergonomic, the LensPen is ideal for the workbench, the range, or in the field.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Lens Pen 48807 The right tool makes even the most difficult or tedious job easier. Enter the compact, two-step Leupold LensPen, which will keep your riflescope and binocular lenses clean and pristine. The LensPen offers a natural hairbrush that's fully retractable when not in use (a clean brush is key because it's the first thing to touch the lens), along with a microfiber cleaning tip that automatically replenishes itself with a state-of-the-art cleaning compound. Overall, the LensPen is far easier and more effective than other lens cleaning methods. Compact and ergonomic, the LensPen is ideal for the workbench, the range, or in the field.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31aVjK7-noL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5H4S.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Gun Scopes", "Rifle Scopes"]], "price": 10.99}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5H7K", "title": "Leupold Rifleman Rf 3/8\"\" Detachable See-Thru Rm Matte 57323", "description": "Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black 3/8-inch detachable see-through ringmounts is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 1.61-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable medium rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Rifleman Rf 3/8\"\" Detachable See-Thru Rm Matte 57323 Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black 3/8-inch detachable see-through ringmounts is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 1.61-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable medium rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41iWqiTZxGL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5H7K.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Paintball & Airsoft", "Airsoft", "Gun Scope Mounts"]], "price": 11.3}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5H8Y", "title": "Leupold Rifleman Detachable See-Thru High Rings Matte 55880", "description": "Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black detachable see-through high rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 1.44-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable medium and high rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Rifleman Detachable See-Thru High Rings Matte 55880 Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black detachable see-through high rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 1.44-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable medium and high rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41ypsyrb6xL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5H8Y.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Paintball & Airsoft", "Airsoft", "Gun Scope Mounts"]], "price": 16.99}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5HA2", "title": "Leupold Rifleman Detachable Medium Rings Matte 55860", "description": "Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black detachable medium rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 0.897-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable see-through rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Rifleman Detachable Medium Rings Matte 55860 Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black detachable medium rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a 0.897-inch size providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable see-through rings, vertical split rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41RkJfCB3AL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5HA2.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Hunting Optics", "Optics Mounts & Bases"]], "price": 16.98}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5HAM", "title": "Leupold Rifleman Vertical Split Rings Matte 55850", "description": "Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black vertical split rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a one-inch tube diameter providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength and recoil resistance you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable see-through rings, detachable medium and high rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "text": "Leupold Rifleman Vertical Split Rings Matte 55850 Leupold mounts are every bit as rugged and dependable as the Leupold optics they're intended to secure. This particular set of matte-black vertical split rings is designed for the Rifleman riflescope, with a one-inch tube diameter providing a snug fit. The rings are extremely affordable--just like the Rifleman scope itself--and are precision machined from aircraft-grade aluminum to provide the strength and recoil resistance you've come to expect without adding excess weight. Leupold also sells a variety of other bases and rings for Rifleman riflescopes, including detachable see-through rings, detachable medium and high rings, and integral see-through mount systems.About LeupoldFrom humble immigrant beginnings, Leupold grew--based on a promise of quality--to become a classic American company. In 1907, Fred Leupold set up a one-man shop at 5th and Oak streets in Portland to repair surveying equipment. He was joined by his brother-in-law, Adam Voelpel, and later by inventor John Cyprian Stevens, and the foundations for a century of success were in place.During Leupold’s second half-century, the company focused heavily on the sports optics business. Leupold’s presence in the hunting and shooting market expanded with innovative optics and features that are now legendary among hunters, shooters, and outdoors enthusiasts. Many of the industry’s standards--nitrogen waterproofing, the Duplex reticle, and more--were Leupold creations.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41Y4sILQoZL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5HAM.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Leupold", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Paintball & Airsoft", "Airsoft", "Gun Scope Mounts"]], "price": 9.14}}
{"item_id": "B001HN5MBQ", "title": "Currie Technologies e-Zip E750 Electric Scooter (Silver)", "description": "Go the distance with ease and speed when you hop aboard the e-Zip 750 Electric Scooter from Currie Technologies, which features both a deck for standing and a removable seat for comfort on longer rides. When you need to go a farther distance than a comfortable walk, the e-Zip 750 will get you there and back quickly thanks to its 12-mile range (depending on rider weight) and top speed of 15 MPH.With increased power of its Currie Electro-Drive system with 750 watts of power matched to a shock absorbing front suspension, it's the perfect choice for serious personal transportation. Other features include an easy on/off seat, folding handlebars for easy trunk stowage, 12.5-inch Street Slick tires, 24-volt/12-ampere-hour Plug & Play rechargeable battery pack, and a Currie Smart battery charger. This scooter is for ages 13 and up, with a maximum rider weight of 260 pounds.Key Features and Specifications:Top speed: 15 MPH (rider weight and terrain contingent)Range: 12 miles (rider weight and terrain contingent)Motor: 750W of power from a DC Earth MagnetController: Exclusive Currie PWM Smart Power Microprocessor 24 Volt fully potted, with relay protection and battery gaugeBattery: EV Rated SLA Type, Plug and Play Design in Nylon Handled Pack, 24V / 12Ah Pack, (2) 12V / 12Ah Valve Regulated, RechargeableDrive: Patented Currie Electro-Drive chain drive systemBrakes: Front linear pull brake with power modulator and alloy brake inhibit leverWheels: Currie polished alloy wide mag wheelsTires: 12.5-inch Currie low profile street slick tires with Tuff-Tire Technology (elastomer subtread reduces chances of flatting)Frame: Hi-Ten steel, heavy duty with one-piece steel tooled battery box and oversized head tubeSaddle: Non-slip ABS resin with in-mold graphics and brand logo badgeWeight: 60 poundsMaximum rider weight: 260 poundsBacked by 90-day manufacturer's warrantyHandlebar: Exclusive Currie folding design and lay forward barsAbout Currie TechnologiesDr. Malcolm Currie, the former chairman of Hughes Aircraft and Delco Electronics, founded Currie Technologies Inc. in 1997 based on his conviction that someday, in the near future, hybrid and electric vehicles would become increasingly important for fundamental economic and environmental reasons. Ten years of sustained experience makes Currie Technologies an acknowledged leader in the business. Its battery technologies include everything from sealed lead acid to nickel metal hydride to the newest and lightest weight lithium-ion battery systems. Currie Technologies utilizes its own factory and design team, who work in conjunction with an international research team to constantly create new designs and respond to market needs.", "text": "Currie Technologies e-Zip E750 Electric Scooter (Silver) Go the distance with ease and speed when you hop aboard the e-Zip 750 Electric Scooter from Currie Technologies, which features both a deck for standing and a removable seat for comfort on longer rides. When you need to go a farther distance than a comfortable walk, the e-Zip 750 will get you there and back quickly thanks to its 12-mile range (depending on rider weight) and top speed of 15 MPH.With increased power of its Currie Electro-Drive system with 750 watts of power matched to a shock absorbing front suspension, it's the perfect choice for serious personal transportation. Other features include an easy on/off seat, folding handlebars for easy trunk stowage, 12.5-inch Street Slick tires, 24-volt/12-ampere-hour Plug & Play rechargeable battery pack, and a Currie Smart battery charger. This scooter is for ages 13 and up, with a maximum rider weight of 260 pounds.Key Features and Specifications:Top speed: 15 MPH (rider weight and terrain contingent)Range: 12 miles (rider weight and terrain contingent)Motor: 750W of power from a DC Earth MagnetController: Exclusive Currie PWM Smart Power Microprocessor 24 Volt fully potted, with relay protection and battery gaugeBattery: EV Rated SLA Type, Plug and Play Design in Nylon Handled Pack, 24V / 12Ah Pack, (2) 12V / 12Ah Valve Regulated, RechargeableDrive: Patented Currie Electro-Drive chain drive systemBrakes: Front linear pull brake with power modulator and alloy brake inhibit leverWheels: Currie polished alloy wide mag wheelsTires: 12.5-inch Currie low profile street slick tires with Tuff-Tire Technology (elastomer subtread reduces chances of flatting)Frame: Hi-Ten steel, heavy duty with one-piece steel tooled battery box and oversized head tubeSaddle: Non-slip ABS resin with in-mold graphics and brand logo badgeWeight: 60 poundsMaximum rider weight: 260 poundsBacked by 90-day manufacturer's warrantyHandlebar: Exclusive Currie folding design and lay forward barsAbout Currie TechnologiesDr. Malcolm Currie, the former chairman of Hughes Aircraft and Delco Electronics, founded Currie Technologies Inc. in 1997 based on his conviction that someday, in the near future, hybrid and electric vehicles would become increasingly important for fundamental economic and environmental reasons. Ten years of sustained experience makes Currie Technologies an acknowledged leader in the business. Its battery technologies include everything from sealed lead acid to nickel metal hydride to the newest and lightest weight lithium-ion battery systems. Currie Technologies utilizes its own factory and design team, who work in conjunction with an international research team to constantly create new designs and respond to market needs.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41vb8cbHHgL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN5MBQ.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Action Sports", "Scooters & Equipment", "Scooters"]]}}
{"item_id": "B001HN6CW4", "title": "NITE IZE S-Biner (3 pk)", "description": "High quality stainless steel constructionAvailable in 6 sizes / 3 finishesSecure stainless steel wire gate closureSize #.5 dimensions: 1.31\" x .5\" weight rating: 3 lb.Size #1 dimensions: 1.56\" x .56\" weight rating: 5 lb.Size #2 dimensions: 2\" x .88\" weight rating: 10 lb.Size #3 dimensions: 2.63\" x 1.13\" weight rating: 25 lb.Size #4 dimensions: 3.5\" x 1.5\" weight rating: 75 lb.Size #5 dimensions: 4.38\" x 1.94\" weight rating: 100 lb.NOT FOR CLIMBING", "text": "NITE IZE S-Biner (3 pk) High quality stainless steel constructionAvailable in 6 sizes / 3 finishesSecure stainless steel wire gate closureSize #.5 dimensions: 1.31\" x .5\" weight rating: 3 lb.Size #1 dimensions: 1.56\" x .56\" weight rating: 5 lb.Size #2 dimensions: 2\" x .88\" weight rating: 10 lb.Size #3 dimensions: 2.63\" x 1.13\" weight rating: 25 lb.Size #4 dimensions: 3.5\" x 1.5\" weight rating: 75 lb.Size #5 dimensions: 4.38\" x 1.94\" weight rating: 100 lb.NOT FOR CLIMBING", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41VOZ7GrMXL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B001HN6CW4.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Nite Ize", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Outdoor Gear", "Climbing", "Carabiners", "Nonlocking"]], "price": 7.89}}
