{"item_id": "B002LVMMBQ", "title": "Bell Lumen Bicycle Road Helmet", "description": "Offering high-end features at an entry level price, the Bell Lumen Bicycle Road Helmet comes with 22 vents for exceptional ventilation. A built-in Geared Positioning System (GPS) delivers one-handed adjustment for a superior fit and added comfort while Cam-Lock strap levers adjust the straps around your ears and face for further fit customization. Other features include a compact shape for an improved aesthetic and CoolMax padding to absorb sweat when the temperature heats up. CE EN178 certified, this helmet comes in three sizes.About BellMore world champions have worn Bell Helmets than all other helmet brands combined. From Grand Prix racing through the Indy 500 to Olympic cycling, Bell helmets have played a vital role in protecting sportsmen and women for nearly 50 years. Bell began as a small auto parts store in a suburb of Los Angeles. Growing under the leadership of Roy Richter, Bell became a leader in safety equipment for auto racing, motorcycling, and then bicycling. His commitment to creating great product through a close connection with the sport, along with his trust of and care for the people who worked for him, turned Bell from a one-man operation into a multi-million dollar enterprise. His legacy lives on today in Bell's commitment to racing, quality and innovation.Helmet Tips--You Should Always...Wear a helmet when you rideWear your helmet low in the front to protect the foreheadFasten your buckle and tighten your chin strapCheck your adjustments every time you wear your helmetInspect your helmet regularly for signs of wear or damageWear a helmet designed for your activity", "text": "Bell Lumen Bicycle Road Helmet Offering high-end features at an entry level price, the Bell Lumen Bicycle Road Helmet comes with 22 vents for exceptional ventilation. A built-in Geared Positioning System (GPS) delivers one-handed adjustment for a superior fit and added comfort while Cam-Lock strap levers adjust the straps around your ears and face for further fit customization. Other features include a compact shape for an improved aesthetic and CoolMax padding to absorb sweat when the temperature heats up. CE EN178 certified, this helmet comes in three sizes.About BellMore world champions have worn Bell Helmets than all other helmet brands combined. From Grand Prix racing through the Indy 500 to Olympic cycling, Bell helmets have played a vital role in protecting sportsmen and women for nearly 50 years. Bell began as a small auto parts store in a suburb of Los Angeles. Growing under the leadership of Roy Richter, Bell became a leader in safety equipment for auto racing, motorcycling, and then bicycling. His commitment to creating great product through a close connection with the sport, along with his trust of and care for the people who worked for him, turned Bell from a one-man operation into a multi-million dollar enterprise. His legacy lives on today in Bell's commitment to racing, quality and innovation.Helmet Tips--You Should Always...Wear a helmet when you rideWear your helmet low in the front to protect the foreheadFasten your buckle and tighten your chin strapCheck your adjustments every time you wear your helmetInspect your helmet regularly for signs of wear or damageWear a helmet designed for your activity", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51JAu0GfT-L._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B002LVMMBQ.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Helmets", "Adult Helmets"]]}}
{"item_id": "B002LVMNLK", "title": "Bell Sequence Bicycle Mountain Helmet", "description": "The Bell Sequence Bicycle Mountain Helmet features aggressive styling and strong lines for cross-country, all-mountain, and XC mountain biking. With in-mold construction and extended full coverage around the rear, the Sequence comes with 20 big vents and internal channels to keep you cool when the temperature rises. Other features include a painted VPV 15-degree adjustable visor for added style and a Twin Axis Gear (TAG) fit system so ensure a snug, comfortable fit.About BellMore world champions have worn Bell Helmets than all other helmet brands combined. From Grand Prix racing through the Indy 500 to Olympic cycling, Bell helmets have played a vital role in protecting sportsmen and women for nearly 50 years. Bell began as a small auto parts store in a suburb of Los Angeles. Growing under the leadership of Roy Richter, Bell became a leader in safety equipment for auto racing, motorcycling, and then bicycling. His commitment to creating great product through a close connection with the sport, along with his trust of and care for the people who worked for him, turned Bell from a one-man operation into a multi-million dollar enterprise. His legacy lives on today in Bell's commitment to racing, quality and innovation.Helmet Tips--You Should Always...Wear a helmet when you rideWear your helmet low in the front to protect the foreheadFasten your buckle and tighten your chin strapCheck your adjustments every time you wear your helmetInspect your helmet regularly for signs of wear or damageWear a helmet designed for your activity", "text": "Bell Sequence Bicycle Mountain Helmet The Bell Sequence Bicycle Mountain Helmet features aggressive styling and strong lines for cross-country, all-mountain, and XC mountain biking. With in-mold construction and extended full coverage around the rear, the Sequence comes with 20 big vents and internal channels to keep you cool when the temperature rises. Other features include a painted VPV 15-degree adjustable visor for added style and a Twin Axis Gear (TAG) fit system so ensure a snug, comfortable fit.About BellMore world champions have worn Bell Helmets than all other helmet brands combined. From Grand Prix racing through the Indy 500 to Olympic cycling, Bell helmets have played a vital role in protecting sportsmen and women for nearly 50 years. Bell began as a small auto parts store in a suburb of Los Angeles. Growing under the leadership of Roy Richter, Bell became a leader in safety equipment for auto racing, motorcycling, and then bicycling. His commitment to creating great product through a close connection with the sport, along with his trust of and care for the people who worked for him, turned Bell from a one-man operation into a multi-million dollar enterprise. His legacy lives on today in Bell's commitment to racing, quality and innovation.Helmet Tips--You Should Always...Wear a helmet when you rideWear your helmet low in the front to protect the foreheadFasten your buckle and tighten your chin strapCheck your adjustments every time you wear your helmetInspect your helmet regularly for signs of wear or damageWear a helmet designed for your activity", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41Sw3h1eufL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B002LVMNLK.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Helmets", "Adult Helmets"]]}}
