{"item_id": "B004XIPSI4", "title": "LaserMax Uni-Max Essential Series Red rail mounted laser with with Integral Rail", "description": "This compact and rugged rail mount laser fits Picatinny; Mil-Spec; Weaver Style Rails (w/ minimum rail length of 1.75\") Battery Type: 357 (2) Accuracy: User-adjusted for windage & elevation Laser Operating Temperature: 5°F - 150°F Wavelength: 650nm (red) Power Output: 5mW Spot Size: 5/16\" @ 7 Yds; 3/4\" @ 25 Yds", "text": "LaserMax Uni-Max Essential Series Red rail mounted laser with with Integral Rail This compact and rugged rail mount laser fits Picatinny; Mil-Spec; Weaver Style Rails (w/ minimum rail length of 1.75\") Battery Type: 357 (2) Accuracy: User-adjusted for windage & elevation Laser Operating Temperature: 5°F - 150°F Wavelength: 650nm (red) Power Output: 5mW Spot Size: 5/16\" @ 7 Yds; 3/4\" @ 25 Yds", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/314GUd9j4aL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B004XIPSI4.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "LaserMax", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Archery", "Accessories", "Bow Maintenance Accessories"]], "price": 119.99}}
{"item_id": "B004XIRH9M", "title": "Four Banger 617 10 Shot Speed Loading Block", "description": "With a Loading Block for the S&W; 617 10 Shot Speedloader you can pre stage your rounds for some fast and fun shooting. A simple push down on the Speedloader clicks in 10 rounds in less than 1 second.... transfer them to the cylinder.... push again and click your 10 empty chambers are full. The average person with a little practice can be reloading their revolver in less than 5 seconds. The Four Banger speed block holds 40 rounds of 22 Long Rifle. If you load 10 rounds in your 617 Speedloader and 40 rounds in the loading block you'll have a total of 50 rounds ready to snap into your revolver. Buy one today and see how fast you can empty it!", "text": "Four Banger 617 10 Shot Speed Loading Block With a Loading Block for the S&W; 617 10 Shot Speedloader you can pre stage your rounds for some fast and fun shooting. A simple push down on the Speedloader clicks in 10 rounds in less than 1 second.... transfer them to the cylinder.... push again and click your 10 empty chambers are full. The average person with a little practice can be reloading their revolver in less than 5 seconds. The Four Banger speed block holds 40 rounds of 22 Long Rifle. If you load 10 rounds in your 617 Speedloader and 40 rounds in the loading block you'll have a total of 50 rounds ready to snap into your revolver. Buy one today and see how fast you can empty it!", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41R9rbVXPnL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B004XIRH9M.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Gun Accessories", "Magazine Loaders"]], "price": 15.95}}
{"item_id": "B004XISGBA", "title": "Ergon GS1 Grip - Leichtbau", "description": "Ergon designed their GS1 grip shape as a perfect medium between their archetypical GP1 grip (the base shape for all GP, GC, and GR series grips) and the race-inspired GX1 grip shape. With the earlier designs on either end of Ergon's size and shape spectrum, the GS1 Leichtbau Grip falls right in-between, offering a shape that works to reduce pressure on your Ulnar nerves and to ease wrist strain while retaining the light weight characteristic of the GX1.We feel like this happy medium will quickly become a favorite for anyone looking to increase their hand comfort on their mountain bike. The wing shaped support is exactly where many glove makers are stitching on extra padding these days, and it provides more support for your hand. You'll perceive less pressure on your palm because of the increased surface area, and the soft kraton rubber gives just enough and allows supreme grip, even with sweat soaked gloves. You'll see a textured rubber insert on the top of the grips. Ergon uses a softer rubber compound here to help dissipate vibration and jolts on the trail.The angle of the grip is important and worth the time to find the position that works best for you. The alloy clamp at the end of the grip should be tightened to a maximum of 5 Nm in order to avoid handlebar damage once you find the right angle. Ergon has found that most people, except those who have huge mitts, go with the small size. The smaller diameter is lighter, a bit stiffer, and easy to grab. Those with big hands and those who spend long, long days in the saddle might want to lean towards large.The Ergon GS1 Leichtbau Grip is available in White and Black and comes in two sizes -- Small and Large. The GS1 is 132mm wide, including the clamp assembly; and it's 54mm front to back at the wing. The set comes with bar plugs and installation instructions.Choosing the correct grip (PDF) Choosing the correct size (PDF) Ergon weight comparison (PDF)", "text": "Ergon GS1 Grip - Leichtbau Ergon designed their GS1 grip shape as a perfect medium between their archetypical GP1 grip (the base shape for all GP, GC, and GR series grips) and the race-inspired GX1 grip shape. With the earlier designs on either end of Ergon's size and shape spectrum, the GS1 Leichtbau Grip falls right in-between, offering a shape that works to reduce pressure on your Ulnar nerves and to ease wrist strain while retaining the light weight characteristic of the GX1.We feel like this happy medium will quickly become a favorite for anyone looking to increase their hand comfort on their mountain bike. The wing shaped support is exactly where many glove makers are stitching on extra padding these days, and it provides more support for your hand. You'll perceive less pressure on your palm because of the increased surface area, and the soft kraton rubber gives just enough and allows supreme grip, even with sweat soaked gloves. You'll see a textured rubber insert on the top of the grips. Ergon uses a softer rubber compound here to help dissipate vibration and jolts on the trail.The angle of the grip is important and worth the time to find the position that works best for you. The alloy clamp at the end of the grip should be tightened to a maximum of 5 Nm in order to avoid handlebar damage once you find the right angle. Ergon has found that most people, except those who have huge mitts, go with the small size. The smaller diameter is lighter, a bit stiffer, and easy to grab. Those with big hands and those who spend long, long days in the saddle might want to lean towards large.The Ergon GS1 Leichtbau Grip is available in White and Black and comes in two sizes -- Small and Large. The GS1 is 132mm wide, including the clamp assembly; and it's 54mm front to back at the wing. The set comes with bar plugs and installation instructions.Choosing the correct grip (PDF) Choosing the correct size (PDF) Ergon weight comparison (PDF)", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51EYgGtCxLL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B004XISGBA.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Cycling", "Parts & Components", "Handlebars, Headsets & Stems", "Handlebars"]]}}
{"item_id": "B004XLAVLK", "title": "MTM Ammo Belt Pouch (Red)", "description": "No more fishing in your pocket for ammo. For the shooter who was always carrying ammo in his pocket. MTM Case-Gard introduces the Ammo Belt Pouch. With a sturdy snap latch and heavy duty belt clip, all you have to do is pour, clip and your ready to shoot. Also a great place to put spent brass. It was designed to hold a 100 rounds of 22 long rifles. Great for target shooting, plinking or small game hunting.", "text": "MTM Ammo Belt Pouch (Red) No more fishing in your pocket for ammo. For the shooter who was always carrying ammo in his pocket. MTM Case-Gard introduces the Ammo Belt Pouch. With a sturdy snap latch and heavy duty belt clip, all you have to do is pour, clip and your ready to shoot. Also a great place to put spent brass. It was designed to hold a 100 rounds of 22 long rifles. Great for target shooting, plinking or small game hunting.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41adKxWJ3bL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B004XLAVLK.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "MTM", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Gun Storage & Safes", "Ammunition & Magazine Pouches"]], "price": 5.99}}
{"item_id": "B004XLAWBE", "title": "MTM 18 Rounds 38 Cal Case-Gard Ammo Wallet (Clear Smoke)", "description": "Looks and feels like a wallet and fits into most pockets. MTM's Handgun Ammo Wallets are great for backup rounds with no rattle noise. Each bullet is held securely and is well-protected. They now come in a See-Thru Smoke Tint. Holds 18 Rounds .38 and .357Mag", "text": "MTM 18 Rounds 38 Cal Case-Gard Ammo Wallet (Clear Smoke) Looks and feels like a wallet and fits into most pockets. MTM's Handgun Ammo Wallets are great for backup rounds with no rattle noise. Each bullet is held securely and is well-protected. They now come in a See-Thru Smoke Tint. Holds 18 Rounds .38 and .357Mag", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/515P3ejxbPL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B004XLAWBE.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Gun Storage & Safes", "Ammunition & Magazine Pouches"]], "price": 7.19}}
